.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Konig, Molenkamp, and coworkers measured a quantized two-terminal conductance of 2e^2/h in HgTe/CdTe quantum wells in 2007 -- the first experimentally realized topological insulator, and the direct confirmation of the band-inverted BHZ model. Opening the BHZ ribbon along one direction with bhz_ribbon_hamiltonian exposes exactly the pair of helical, counter-propagating edge states carrying that dissipationless conductance: gapless at k_x=0, spin-locked, and immune to backscattering by nonmagnetic disorder.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/condensed/topology/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_qsh_edge_states_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/condensed/topology/plot_qsh_edge_states`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Quantum Spin Hall Effect: Konig et al.'s Helical Edge States</div>
